rm that very quickly could  get out of control  heather urex west global news calgary  blaming poor intelligence and each other  coming up  why didn't those in charge of security  on capitol hill anticipate  the violent riot plus a fireball erupts  after an  explosive crash  there is a blame game playing out in  washington tonight about the deadly  capitol hill riots on january 6th  a hearing is underway into the violent  siege and officials in charge of  security  testified publicly for the first time as  jackson proskow reports they are  pointing the finger at bad intelligence  and a delayed federal response these  criminals came prepared for war  they came with their own radio system to  coordinate the attack and climbing gear  and other equipment to defeat the  capital's security features  in chilling detail those tasked with  securing the u.s capitol building  described the highly coordinated attack  they faced at the hands of pro-trump  rioters  i received chemical burns to my face  that still have not healed to this day  after an impeachment that focused on the  words and actions of president donald  trump  the reckoning has moved on to security  lapses  during the attack as the capital was  overtaken washington's police chief says  the pentagon was reluctant to deploy the  national guard  concerned about the optics of using  troops and my response to that  was simply i was just stunned that you  know i have officers that were out there  literally fighting for their lives  the chief of the capitol police and the  sergeants at arms who have all since  resigned  insist they prepared for that day based  on the intelligence they had  we all believed that the plan met the  threat  and that we were prepared we now know  that we had the wrong plan  the day before the attack an fbi  intelligence bulletin warned protesters  were ready for war  what we got was a military-style  coordinated assault on my officers  and a violent takeover of the capitol  building concerned about our election  integrity  while to this day some republican  senators continue to deflect from their  own role  in pushing lies about a stolen election  floating discredited theories  that the mob was actually made up of  fake trump supporters  there is however bipartisan agreements  on the need to improve capital security  permanently at a hearing on monday  president joe biden's nominee for  attorney general warned the threat of  domestic extremism  is at its highest level in decades donna  all right jackson proskow in washington  thanks  deal reached ahead why facebook is  lifting its ban on news  in australia  this frightening inferno happened in  texas this morning an 18-wheeler  collided with a train carrying coal and  gasoline  the huge explosion sent dark smoke high  into the sky  at least one home was destroyed no one  was hurt  the cause is under investigation  australia has scored a victory in its  drive to make internet giants pay for  news and for the work of journalists  facebook has agreed to lift its ban on  australians viewing and sharing news on  its platform  the social media company struck a deal  with the government on a bill designed  to  force platforms like facebook and google  to share ad revenue with news outlets  last week facebook removed all news  content for its australian users that  provoked outrage  countries around the world have kept a  close eye on the dispute including  canada  there are reports the federal government  has agreed to coordinate efforts with  australia to ensure  social media companies here also pay for  journalism  doctors orders get outside next  prescribing nature  for healing  the duke of edinburgh will spend a few  more days in the hospital in london  buckingham palace has revealed prince  philip has an infection and is  comfortable in responding to treatment  but is not expected to leave the  hospital for several days  the 99 year old husband of the queen was  admitted to king edward vii  hospital a week ago well it's well known  that getting outside can be good for  your health  it's called forest bathing or ecotherapy  it's not an alternative treatment for  serious disease of course but it is a  healing idea  that is catching on robin gill explains  the west coast has the advantage of  milder weather than the rest of canada  so it's easy for carmen ruazi laza to  get up for a walk  rain or shine it's getting me into  better condition  not just physically emotionally  spiritually and  definitely mentally as well that caught  the attention of dr melissa lem  a family physician for more than a  decade she started writing  formal prescriptions for her patients to  get outside  why is a prescription better than just  telling your patient  well there is evidence showing that  written prescriptions are better  received  than just verbal advice at motivating  patients to make a change  during a patient call or visit dr lem  custom prescribes nature prescriptions  depending on a person's condition  whether there's a chronic disease or  mental health issues i think they  understand intuitively that nature is  good for them  and so sometimes it just takes that  little reminder from a physician  the prescription initiative recommends  two hours in nature per week  and one session should be at least 20  minutes because that's how long it takes  for stress levels to drop  british columbia is the first to start  this program in canada  ontario has now signed up the university  of calgary  and university of alberta are joining  forces on a study  that seems obvious to nature lovers  nature can be in your front yard it can  be in your backyard  you know there's great data out there  that says just looking at nature  is is enough to sort of calm that  parasympathetic nervous system and relax  you  and to refocus your attention dr lem  knows it herself  it's been said that doctors should not  self-prescribe but in this situation  would you self-prescribe  that's a good question i i think i feel  my prescription almost every single day  i make sure that i get outside for at  least half an hour into nature every day  and then there's carmen ruaz elaza she's  already in tune with the effect of  bathing in nature  it just calms everything down that  healthy dose of fresh air keeps her  coming outside for an hour  every day robin gill global news  vancouver  that is global national for this tuesday  i'm donna friesen well cute animal  videos can be good for the health too  and  there's no shortage of those here's one  police in charlottetown were called to  help this seal it was wandering around a  neighborhood obviously lost  the officers popped it in the back of  the car and gave it a lift  back to the sea it slid back to its  natural habitat  thanks for watching hope to see you here  again tomorrow take care of yourselves  [Music]  bye  [Music]  you
 

